Normalization is conservative: a code block containing a nested code
block passes through byte-for-byte, while the surrounding statement is
still spaced (fmt.code_block_literals bail-outs). (The multi-line-body
bail-out is left out: inside a procedure, range-formatting its second
line re-indents it, an invariant failure reported separately.)
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Nested;
:DECLARE fnOuter, vResult;
fnOuter:={|x|Eval({|y|y+1}, x)};
vResult:=Eval(fnOuter,1);
:RETURN vResult;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Nested;
	:DECLARE fnOuter, vResult;
	fnOuter := {|x|Eval({|y|y+1}, x)};
	vResult := Eval(fnOuter, 1);
	:RETURN vResult;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
